From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:14:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v41: run on four DGX Sparks (TP=4)

- tensor-parallel block partitions: every split on whole 128-wide Hadamard
  blocks; even where possible (all TP2 shapes are unchanged), otherwise the
  first ranks take one more block (experts 640/640/512/512, vocabulary
  32,384/32,384/32,256/32,256)
- the engine, family factory and CLI take --tp 4 / --rank 0..3; every rank
  agreement, the session-tier key intersection and the sampler's candidate
  gather run over world ranks
- the TCP round-plan link broadcasts to every follower
- RoCE all-gather: each proxy starts its posts at the next rank (no incast)
- package the csa2 CUDA sources (attn_cuda / topk_cuda were not installed)
- prefill: count routed pairs without torch.bincount's host sync
- /health and /metrics: drafted_total / accepted_total from the DSpark and
  lookup drafts (were always 0 for this family)
- TF_DSV41_PREFILL_PROFILE: an opt-in profile of one prompt prefill
- tests/test_dsv41_tp4.py: four ranks on threads (uneven partitions, == one
  rank in exact numerics, ranks agree bit for bit, row invariance, greedy
  over uneven vocabulary slices, Engram from of4 shards)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WAyL9TFbTLwjeNsrEKfKAF
